williemm wrote:
> Little White Mouse makes a very interesting point that the blue jelly
> room is a form of death and not really living.

After monster generation has stopped (remember the extinction counter),
the difference is academical, and we are talking about eternity here.
Even a horn of plenty is guaranteed to give you a streak of acid potions
long enough to let you starve (assuming a perfect RNG), brown puddings
are guaranteed to leave a long streak of non-corpses and black puddings
or summon nasties (which doesn't respect extinction) might kill you,
even at an AC of -127 and 16k HP. So all that is left seems to be the
ring trick, or praying with low-enough luck.

